{
  // The shipped code, held to one rule the editor configuration does not:
  // `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`. An index into an array or a record can miss,
  // and without this the type says it cannot.
  //
  // Two functions in this repository were typed to return a value and returned
  // `undefined`: `ruleSetById` for a variant no longer known, `currentPlayer`
  // for a stale turn index. Each made a chat throw on every command, forever,
  // three files from the row that was wrong. This is the flag that would have
  // said so at the keyboard.
  //
  // Tests are deliberately out of scope. `rows[0]` in a test is a value the
  // test constructed two lines earlier, and a guard there adds noise without
  // adding truth.
  //
  // And two flags the editor does not turn on either. `noUnusedLocals` is what
  // would have caught three functions in `packages/db/src/legacy.ts` — dead the
  // moment `stateFromLegacy` began delegating, and invisible to everything:
  // `audit-unread` reads exports and fields, and a private function is neither.
  // They were found by hand, a pass later, only because one of them had been
  // copied. `noUnusedParameters` is its other half: an argument nothing reads
  // is a question the caller was asked and nobody answered.
  //
  // Tests are out of scope here for the reason above: a helper written for one
  // test and left is noise, not a defect.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": true,
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    "noUnusedParameters": true,
    // No Node globals in the browser bundle. `scripts/` and `tests/` get them
    // from the configuration above; `src/` is what ships, and `process` in it
    // is a mistake that should not typecheck.
    "types": ["vite/client"]
  },
  "include": ["src"]
}
